krdp 6.6.7: the Plasma session asks KWin for a stream again, upstream's
"Fix plasma screencast option" (429f584c, 2026-03-31, which the 6.6
releases don't have) rebased onto v6.6.7, plus the server side of it,
which upstream changed on its own: SessionController hands the session
a monitor index only when --monitor gave one. In 6.6.7 the server
hands each session the --monitor index, -1 when none was given, and
PlasmaScreencastV1Session::start() creates its workspace stream only
when that index is zero: with no --monitor it requests nothing, and
the client connects to an empty screen (nothing in the log past "Video
stream initialized" but two "QObject::connect(...): invalid nullptr
parameter"). The fix keeps the index optional, streams the named
monitor when there is one and the whole workspace otherwise. With the
session's half alone the -1 reaches screens().at(-1) and the server
segfaults in QScreen::handle() as the client connects.

diff --color -u -r a/server/SessionController.cpp b/server/SessionController.cpp
--- a/server/SessionController.cpp
+++ b/server/SessionController.cpp
@@ -133,8 +133,8 @@
     auto wrapper = std::make_unique<SessionWrapper>(newConnection, makeSession(), m_sni);
     if (m_virtualMonitor) {
         wrapper->session->setVirtualMonitor(*m_virtualMonitor);
-    } else {
-        wrapper->session->setActiveStream(m_monitorIndex.value_or(-1));
+    } else if (m_monitorIndex) {
+        wrapper->session->setActiveStream(*m_monitorIndex);
     }
     wrapper->session->setVideoQuality(m_quality.value());
 
